From: yonto-app <336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:45:02 +1300
Subject: [PATCH] input: es_out: give an ES an id no other ES holds

An ES whose demuxer gives it no id takes the count of ES added so far.
A demuxer that numbers its own ES from its streams (asf, from 1) can
already hold that number, so a subtitle file added beside a WMV took
the audio track's id. Selecting it by that id (spu-es, or a slave
added with select) finds the audio ES first, which is already
selected, so the subtitles were listed and reported as selected but
never decoded.

The counted id now moves past any id an ES already holds.

Message-Id: <b433d89081a527390a1619506e7dbd8f440406c5.1795416302.git.336298264+yonto-app@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/input/es_out.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/input/es_out.c b/src/input/es_out.c
--- a/src/input/es_out.c
+++ b/src/input/es_out.c
@@ -1557,7 +1557,14 @@ static es_out_id_t *EsOutAddSlave( es_out_t *out, const es_format_t *fmt, es_out_id_t *p_master )
     es->p_pgrm = p_pgrm;
     es_format_Copy( &es->fmt, fmt );
     if( es->fmt.i_id < 0 )
+    {
+        /* A demuxer that numbers its own ES (asf) can already hold the
+         * counted id, and an ES given it could never be selected: an id
+         * finds the first ES that has it. */
         es->fmt.i_id = p_sys->i_id;
+        while( EsOutGetFromID( out, es->fmt.i_id ) != NULL )
+            es->fmt.i_id++;
+    }
     if( !es->fmt.i_original_fourcc )
         es->fmt.i_original_fourcc = es->fmt.i_codec;
 
